Benchmark-only hook for Mirage MPK (branch mpk, 2edbcf40), used by mirage_layers.py.

It changes neither what Mirage computes nor how it schedules; it only chooses how many decode
steps one offline-mode launch runs and from which position:
  * -DMPK_BENCH_DECODE=<Q> (passed through the MPK_EXTRA_NVCC_FLAGS hook in persistent_kernel.py):
    a newly admitted request starts at step prompt_length - Q, its pages covering
    [0, prompt_length) (the KV rows before it are taken as already cached), so the first
    iteration computes the last Q tokens: a decode step at context prompt_length.  Decode
    iterations then feed Q tokens (Q = 1 here, the stock value).
  * mpk_bench_set_steps(n) (host function, ctypes): with n > 0 the request finishes after n such
    steps; n = 0 keeps the stock termination rule (max_seq_length / EOS).
Apply: git -C <mirage checkout at origin/mpk> apply mirage_mpk_bench.patch

